WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.312 --> 00:00:03.105
(exploding)

00:00:03.105 --> 00:00:03.965
- What's up, Believe Nation?

00:00:03.965 --> 00:00:05.971
It's Evan, my one word is "believe,"

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:07.447
and I believe that you have

00:00:07.447 --> 00:00:09.164
the ability to do something special

00:00:09.164 --> 00:00:11.745
and I'm trying to help have a small impact

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.834
on your growth with these videos.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.305
And so to help you on your journey,

00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:17.973
today we're continuing
the Best of Tony series,

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:19.650
where we look at some of the best clips

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.401
that Tony Robinson's come up with.

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:25.048
Today's theme is "believe,"
and I hope you enjoy.

00:00:25.048 --> 00:00:26.684
- Think about it, what's the Holy Grail

00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:28.766
between somebody taking action or not?

00:00:28.766 --> 00:00:31.301
It's one word: certainty.

00:00:31.301 --> 00:00:33.223
When somebody is absolutely certain they,

00:00:33.223 --> 00:00:35.268
the common word is "believe," right?

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.580
But you know, you can
believe at a general level

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:37.479
or you can believe with certainty.

00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:39.482
When you're absolutely
certain that if I do this,

00:00:39.482 --> 00:00:40.953
it's going to get that
result, and that result's

00:00:40.953 --> 00:00:43.655
going to change my life, you'll do it.

00:00:43.655 --> 00:00:46.273
When you think, "It absolutely
is not going to work,"

00:00:46.273 --> 00:00:47.714
you're never going to do it.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.707
The middle no man's land
of "Maybe it'll work,

00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:53.690
maybe it won't," that's the
piece that kills people.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.837
So if it's a must for you,
you got to make it work.

00:00:56.837 --> 00:00:59.172
In our case, right, it's an example.

00:00:59.172 --> 00:01:01.262
If it's not a must for
you and you're not sure,

00:01:01.262 --> 00:01:02.095
you don't know what to do.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.687
So years ago I'd look around and say,

00:01:03.687 --> 00:01:05.161
"Okay, how do people get themselves

00:01:05.161 --> 00:01:06.916
to follow through that haven't
been following through?

00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:07.749
What's the difference?"

00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:10.144
And I started interviewing
hundreds of people, literally.

00:01:10.144 --> 00:01:11.170
And eventually thousands,

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.398
'cause I had thousands at my events,

00:01:12.398 --> 00:01:14.316
so I'd ask the group to
give me their feedback.

00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:15.258
And I came up with this model.

00:01:15.258 --> 00:01:17.215
It's like the Holy Grail of belief.

00:01:17.215 --> 00:01:19.022
Or the Holy Grail of momentum.

00:01:19.022 --> 00:01:20.498
It's like the difference between

00:01:20.498 --> 00:01:21.774
what makes the rich get richer

00:01:21.774 --> 00:01:23.376
and the poor get poorer, right?

00:01:23.376 --> 00:01:24.891
And the difference, we
all know, is mindset,

00:01:24.891 --> 00:01:26.077
but like, how's that built?

00:01:26.077 --> 00:01:26.982
So this is what I did.

00:01:26.982 --> 00:01:28.581
I created these stupid
little, four little boxes.

00:01:28.581 --> 00:01:30.787
And I'll scribble it here for you.

00:01:30.787 --> 00:01:31.975
You think about the first thing

00:01:31.975 --> 00:01:33.941
that determines whether you
can do something or not.

00:01:33.941 --> 00:01:35.544
And I put that in this first box

00:01:35.544 --> 00:01:36.817
at the top here on the left side.

00:01:36.817 --> 00:01:37.798
It's potential.

00:01:37.798 --> 00:01:39.763
Like what's the potential
of a human being?

00:01:39.763 --> 00:01:42.305
Like when you guys started, you proved

00:01:42.305 --> 00:01:43.492
something no one had done in history.

00:01:43.492 --> 00:01:45.295
You ran the four-minute mile, right?

00:01:45.295 --> 00:01:46.771
For golly-knows how many centuries,

00:01:46.771 --> 00:01:47.877
they're trying to run a four-minute mile.

00:01:47.877 --> 00:01:50.742
Roger Bannister does it, how did he do it?

00:01:50.742 --> 00:01:52.085
Do you remember?

00:01:52.085 --> 00:01:53.112
You did it in this industry, right?

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.874
You made a million bucks in a day.

00:01:54.874 --> 00:01:56.765
No one had ever done
that in history, right?

00:01:56.765 --> 00:01:58.812
After you did it a bunch
of other guys are doing it,

00:01:58.812 --> 00:02:00.167
because it became possible.

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.539
Roger Bannister didn't just
go physically practice.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.258
He made a shift in his head.

00:02:04.258 --> 00:02:05.283
He practiced in his head,

00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:07.249
'cause he could never
achieve it physically,

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:08.805
so he had to change in his head first

00:02:08.805 --> 00:02:10.322
so the result became certain enough,

00:02:10.322 --> 00:02:12.745
he believed it, and then
his body got him through.

00:02:12.745 --> 00:02:15.619
After Roger Bannister ran
that four-minute mile,

00:02:15.619 --> 00:02:18.452
within two years, 37 people
ran a four-minute mile.

00:02:18.452 --> 00:02:19.285
- Wow.
- That's amazing.

00:02:19.285 --> 00:02:20.502
- When no one in history had ever done.

00:02:20.502 --> 00:02:21.650
Now here's how it works.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.170
The potential for anybody getting

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.400
your product is extraordinary.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.904
They could do what you've
done, as much more or less.

00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:28.296
They can do whatever they want to do.

00:02:28.296 --> 00:02:31.291
The potential's there,
the market's proven that.

00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:32.930
Whether or not they
tap into that potential

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.407
has a lot to do with
what action they take,

00:02:34.407 --> 00:02:37.088
which is the question
that came to me, right?

00:02:37.088 --> 00:02:38.919
They got all this potential
but they're not taking action.

00:02:38.919 --> 00:02:40.923
And we all know that the action they take

00:02:40.923 --> 00:02:43.176
is going to determine
the results they get.

00:02:43.176 --> 00:02:44.610
That's pretty obvious.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.943
So most people have a belief

00:02:48.341 --> 00:02:49.855
about what their real potential is,

00:02:49.855 --> 00:02:51.451
no matter what you tell them.

00:02:51.451 --> 00:02:53.575
And that affects how
much action they take.

00:02:53.575 --> 00:02:54.928
And of course, that affects the result.

00:02:54.928 --> 00:02:59.609
And then, ironically, that
result reinforces their belief.

00:02:59.609 --> 00:03:00.592
And then that belief affects it.

00:03:00.592 --> 00:03:02.354
So I'll give you an example.

00:03:02.354 --> 00:03:06.522
Let's say a person has unlimited
potential, we all agree.

00:03:06.522 --> 00:03:09.022
But they take little
action, little results, why?

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.318
'Cause they have to start with
a problem with their belief.

00:03:11.318 --> 00:03:13.574
They don't believe it's
really going to happen for me.

00:03:13.574 --> 00:03:14.557
"Maybe for Frank Kern,

00:03:14.557 --> 00:03:16.071
'cause he's got the cool hair and stuff,

00:03:16.071 --> 00:03:18.236
or maybe it's for you,
because you're so driven.

00:03:18.236 --> 00:03:19.260
But it's not me.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.981
Maybe Tony Robbins,
'cause he's he's a freak,

00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:21.814
got these big teeth,"

00:03:21.814 --> 00:03:22.655
whatever their thought process
(laughter)

00:03:22.655 --> 00:03:24.534
is, they got this thing, right?

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:27.430
But what happens is, if you believe

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.586
that there's very little potential,

00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:31.466
how much action you going to take?

00:03:31.466 --> 00:03:32.299
- Nothing.

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:33.197
- Nothing, little.

00:03:33.197 --> 00:03:35.119
And when you take little
potential with little action,

00:03:35.119 --> 00:03:37.002
what kind of results do you get?

00:03:37.002 --> 00:03:37.985
Lousy little results.

00:03:37.985 --> 00:03:38.830
And when you get little results,

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.229
what does that do to your belief?

00:03:40.229 --> 00:03:42.521
You go, "See, I told you
this was a waste of time.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.151
Told you this wouldn't work."

00:03:44.151 --> 00:03:46.156
And then what happens, you
tap even less potential,

00:03:46.156 --> 00:03:48.166
you take even less action,
you get even worse results,

00:03:48.166 --> 00:03:49.766
and your belief gets even weaker.

00:03:49.766 --> 00:03:51.197
And this sucker feeds on itself

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.955
until you are in a downward spiral

00:03:52.955 --> 00:03:53.858
- [Frank] It's poisonous.

00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:55.943
- It's poisonous and it's self-fulfilling.

00:03:55.943 --> 00:03:57.293
Now, what if something could happen

00:03:57.293 --> 00:03:59.344
that could come along and fill you

00:03:59.344 --> 00:04:01.231
with a sense of absolute certainty?

00:04:01.231 --> 00:04:04.214
Not like, "I believe," but where you know.

00:04:04.214 --> 00:04:08.382
In you guys' case, mine as
well, we knew 'cause we had to.

00:04:08.382 --> 00:04:10.391
'Cause we burned the boats,
there was no other option.

00:04:10.391 --> 00:04:11.779
We had to find a way.

00:04:11.779 --> 00:04:13.545
We weren't going to live that way.

00:04:13.545 --> 00:04:15.465
We all did it in different
ways and for different reasons,

00:04:15.465 --> 00:04:17.102
but in essence, that was it.

00:04:17.102 --> 00:04:19.718
If you get yourself in
a state of certainty

00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:21.316
that this is going to work,
I'm going to find a way,

00:04:21.316 --> 00:04:23.488
and if this doesn't work,
I will make the way,

00:04:23.488 --> 00:04:26.102
then you tap a lot more potential.

00:04:26.102 --> 00:04:27.491
And when you're certain in your potential

00:04:27.491 --> 00:04:29.045
you take massive action.

00:04:29.045 --> 00:04:30.316
And when you take massive action,

00:04:30.316 --> 00:04:32.573
you really believe in something,
you get great results.

00:04:32.573 --> 00:04:33.721
When you get great results,

00:04:33.721 --> 00:04:36.424
your brain goes, "See,
I told you I was a stud.

00:04:36.424 --> 00:04:37.773
I told you this thing would work out."

00:04:37.773 --> 00:04:38.913
Now you're even stronger.

00:04:38.913 --> 00:04:40.097
You tap more potential,
take greater action,

00:04:40.097 --> 00:04:41.036
get greater results.

00:04:41.036 --> 00:04:42.920
That's how you went
from 300 bucks in a week

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.645
to 2500 in five days,
to 100,000 in a month,

00:04:46.645 --> 00:04:48.035
to a million bucks in a day.

00:04:48.035 --> 00:04:49.142
Same thing with you.

00:04:49.142 --> 00:04:50.209
And we get momentum.

00:04:50.209 --> 00:04:52.086
It's why the rich get richer
and the poor get poorer.

00:04:52.086 --> 00:04:53.394
Now some people go out and they go,

00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:55.197
"Well, I'm going to take a
bunch of action, alright?

00:04:55.197 --> 00:04:57.001
I'm going to open this
product, I'm going to try it,"

00:04:57.001 --> 00:04:58.924
and they'll say to you, "I even did it."

00:04:58.924 --> 00:05:00.644
But it's like a salesman who
goes and knocks on the door

00:05:00.644 --> 00:05:02.897
and he knocks on 100 doors and says,

00:05:02.897 --> 00:05:04.370
- You don't want one of these, do you?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.267
- Yeah, exactly right.
(laughter)

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:06.456
And even if he doesn't say it verbally,

00:05:06.456 --> 00:05:09.495
his face says it because he
doesn't believe it's going to work,

00:05:09.495 --> 00:05:13.111
so his voice, his body,
the execution, is so weak.

00:05:13.111 --> 00:05:15.558
If he talks to 100 people,
somebody's going to buy out of pity.

00:05:15.558 --> 00:05:17.116
They don't want his kids to starve, right?

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.511
But he's not going to get the result.

00:05:18.511 --> 00:05:20.279
So the core difference in people is,

00:05:20.279 --> 00:05:22.321
how do you produce certainty

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.487
when the world isn't giving it to you?

00:05:24.487 --> 00:05:26.407
You go out and you try
and you try, in your case,

00:05:26.407 --> 00:05:28.416
you're 100,000 in debt
and nothing's working.

00:05:28.416 --> 00:05:29.604
How do you keep yourself going?

00:05:29.604 --> 00:05:31.233
The way you did it, the way I did it,

00:05:31.233 --> 00:05:32.466
the way you're doing it,

00:05:32.466 --> 00:05:34.027
we may not have done it consciously,

00:05:34.027 --> 00:05:36.890
is, we didn't change our
potential, that was there.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.104
And it wasn't even taking more action.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.210
Taking more action with a belief

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.461
that's not going to work's
not going to change anything.

00:05:42.461 --> 00:05:46.235
We got results in our head
that made us feel certain,

00:05:46.235 --> 00:05:47.712
as if it had already happened.

00:05:47.712 --> 00:05:48.650
True or false for you?

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:49.483
- True.

00:05:49.483 --> 00:05:50.491
- Right, so give me an example.

00:05:50.491 --> 00:05:52.289
So people know I'm not
just making this crap up.

00:05:52.289 --> 00:05:54.418
- Well, I mean, just
like when I had nothing,

00:05:54.418 --> 00:05:56.509
I already knew I was driving like Ferraris

00:05:56.509 --> 00:05:58.794
and Porsches and stuff 'cause
I always wanted those cars.

00:05:58.794 --> 00:06:01.095
I already knew I was going to have them.

00:06:01.095 --> 00:06:01.946
It was inevitable.

00:06:01.946 --> 00:06:03.379
- [Tony] Right.

00:06:03.379 --> 00:06:04.776
- [Frank] That was just
my inevitable outcome.

00:06:04.776 --> 00:06:05.636
- But how did you do that?

00:06:05.636 --> 00:06:07.492
Did you have a ritual, did
you think about it regularly?

00:06:07.492 --> 00:06:08.884
Was it one time you thought about it

00:06:08.884 --> 00:06:11.143
or was it something you
had an obsession towards?

00:06:11.143 --> 00:06:12.332
- I had an obsession towards it.

00:06:12.332 --> 00:06:14.233
I used to work at a video store,

00:06:14.233 --> 00:06:16.120
which is the last "job"
I ever had in my life.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:16.953
- Thank god.

00:06:16.953 --> 00:06:19.719
- And I used to go to
work almost every day,

00:06:19.719 --> 00:06:21.844
and I used to bring two magazines

00:06:21.844 --> 00:06:23.645
with me to read on my breaks.

00:06:23.645 --> 00:06:25.084
Entrepreneur Magazine, just to read

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.316
about business and everything else,

00:06:26.316 --> 00:06:27.417
to read about what other people are doing,

00:06:27.417 --> 00:06:28.603
look for role models.

00:06:28.603 --> 00:06:30.731
And I used to carry an Autotrader with me.

00:06:30.731 --> 00:06:33.311
And I used to look at
Porsches that were for sale.

00:06:33.311 --> 00:06:34.867
And people always used to ask me,

00:06:34.867 --> 00:06:36.835
"What are you doing with
that Autotrader magazine?"

00:06:36.835 --> 00:06:38.432
I'm like, "Well, I'm just
picking out the Porsche

00:06:38.432 --> 00:06:39.600
that I'm going to buy when I'm--"

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.608
- Right, which probably
got you a lot of crap.

00:06:41.608 --> 00:06:42.711
- It did.

00:06:42.711 --> 00:06:44.021
People made fun of me.

00:06:44.021 --> 00:06:46.643
I actually had a boss at that job tell me,

00:06:46.643 --> 00:06:49.468
"You know, you really shouldn't
do that to yourself, John.

00:06:49.468 --> 00:06:51.630
Because it's very, very likely

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.026
that that is never going to happen.

00:06:53.026 --> 00:06:57.178
It's very likely that you're
never going to have that car."

00:06:57.178 --> 00:06:59.772
that's the kind of belief he
was trying to put in my head.

00:06:59.772 --> 00:07:01.662
And I was like, "No, you don't realize

00:07:01.662 --> 00:07:05.102
that it's inevitable
that I will drive here

00:07:05.102 --> 00:07:07.153
sometime in the near future with that car,

00:07:07.153 --> 00:07:09.073
when I'm not working for you,

00:07:09.073 --> 00:07:12.353
and drop movies off for you
to put back on the shelf."

00:07:12.353 --> 00:07:13.745
- And anybody wants to succeed

00:07:13.745 --> 00:07:16.079
has got to know, it doesn't just happen.

00:07:16.079 --> 00:07:17.758
You can buy a product, but you also,

00:07:17.758 --> 00:07:20.096
with that product, have
got to condition yourself.

00:07:20.096 --> 00:07:22.471
You got to make it a must
and you got to get a ritual.

00:07:22.471 --> 00:07:24.315
And if you do it, whatever
you used to dream about

00:07:24.315 --> 00:07:25.907
that you thought was so
huge, you'll just live it.

00:07:25.907 --> 00:07:27.340
You'll live it like you
lived this yesterday,

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.179
like we're living the
life that we envisioned.

00:07:29.179 --> 00:07:31.432
'Cause we had to, and 'cause we played

00:07:31.432 --> 00:07:32.579
this game with our head.

00:07:32.579 --> 00:07:35.442
We got the belief to be real
by seeing it enough times

00:07:35.442 --> 00:07:37.651
and feeling it enough times
'til our brain believed it

00:07:37.651 --> 00:07:38.797
and then it made it happen.

00:07:38.797 --> 00:07:39.741
- Which raised the potential,

00:07:39.741 --> 00:07:41.010
which made us take more action,

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.118
which got us better results,

00:07:42.118 --> 00:07:43.469
which raised our beliefs again.

00:07:43.469 --> 00:07:44.302
- That's right.

00:07:44.302 --> 00:07:45.561
And then that's why the rich get richer

00:07:45.561 --> 00:07:46.753
and the poor get poorer.

00:07:46.753 --> 00:07:48.926
So instead of bitching
about it, change it.

00:07:48.926 --> 00:07:51.921
This process is the Holy Grail.

00:07:51.921 --> 00:07:53.399
It's where the whole game changes.

00:07:53.399 --> 00:07:55.525
And anybody can do it, and they
can do it in a few minutes,

00:07:55.525 --> 00:07:57.699
and if they do it a few minutes each day,

00:07:57.699 --> 00:07:59.051
then they get a different life.

00:07:59.051 --> 00:08:00.651
They do it a few minutes one time,

00:08:00.651 --> 00:08:02.826
their life changes for the day.

00:08:02.826 --> 00:08:04.639
We're defined by our rituals.

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:06.571
Everybody's got rituals, certain
things they do every day.

00:08:06.571 --> 00:08:07.883
And what we three have in common

00:08:07.883 --> 00:08:09.441
and anybody that I know of who has a life

00:08:09.441 --> 00:08:12.220
that they're living
that was once a vision,

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.067
is we saw it again and again and again,

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:16.400
even when it didn't work,
even when you lost 100 grand,

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.166
even when I'm working as a janitor.

00:08:18.166 --> 00:08:20.670
There was something we
would not give up on.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.307
And if somebody watching
wants to change their life,

00:08:22.307 --> 00:08:24.146
they got to decide what
they won't give up on

00:08:24.146 --> 00:08:25.577
and then put themselves in this state

00:08:25.577 --> 00:08:27.455
of momentum by a couple little rituals.

